adr: 0215
file: selfhost/apfront.pas
kills: typeinquiry_access_errors
why: 6.5.6's substring-variable is a variable-access, so AP 6.4.9 admits it syntactically, and what it possesses is 6.4.3.3.1's canonical-string-type -- a pointer and a length with no storage behind them. A variable cannot have it. Without the test the declaration is accepted and nothing complains until the program runs: `a string of length 3 does not fit a capacity of 0`, at the first assignment, which is how this was found. The compile-time answer is the only one a golden holds, so only a case naming the message can see it.
--- old
  else if d^.tqObj^.ntype = canonStringType then begin
--- new
  else if false then begin
